Kutafin Moscow State Law University (MSAL) (before until 2012 – Moscow State Law Academy – MSAL) is a recognized leader of a quality teaching and research in various areas of law in the Russian Federation.
Since its foundation, the Kutafin Moscow State Law University (MSAL) has trained many generations of highly qualified experts in a variety of law disciplines who are well-equipped and ever-prepared to tackle most challenging problems of modern legal science.
The number of its students in Moscow and in its five branches in other cities is about 15 000 including over 500 postgraduate students pursuing Candidate (Ph.D.) and Doctor of Law Degrees.
The Kutafin Moscow State Law University (MSAL) has ten Departments teaching law (among them there is Department of Energy Law, one of the first in Russia), 31 chairs with over 1000 teaching staff, including about 190 professors many of whom are well known in the international legal community.
