Light steel keel or aluminum alloy keel is used, and the ceiling grid is installed according to the specifications of the selected sound-absorbing board, and then the mineral fiber ceiling board is directly placed on the ceiling grid, which is used for the installation of non-grooving and narrow-side drop-down boards. The characteristics of this installation method are relatively simple and convenient for maintenance and replacement.
The ceiling grid is divided into main tee, long cross tee, short cross tee and wall angle. The middle one is 3.6 meters long, the middle one is 1.2 meters long, the minor one is 0.6 meters long, and the corner one is 3 meters long.
The ceiling grid is made of cold-rolled continuous hot-dip galvanized steel strip and paint-coated steel strip as raw materials, through the cold bending process, composite rolling into a reasonable "T" shaped section structure thin-walled section.
It has the advantages of light weight, high strength, waterproof, fireproof, shockproof, sound insulation, sound absorption, etc. It also has the advantages of short construction period and simple construction.
