To limit the spread of covid-19 on its territory, France has established a red list of countries where it is forbidden to go except for compelling reasons. As of Monday, a total of seven African countries are now included.
Thus, Tunisia and Mozambique join the French list of countries where covid-19 is actively circulating, along with Indonesia and Cuba. They will join five other African countries that were already on this list, namely: South Africa, Namibia, DRC, Seychelles and Zambia.
In Tunisia, the virulence of the new variant is causing concern among public authorities because of its impact on the health system. Tuesday, July 6, the country recorded 9823 cases, including 134 deaths in one day, a record since March 2020.
