In the light of recent political developments in the DRC - end of the Tshisekedi-Kabila coalition, new government of "thesacred union»- We can see how Dan Gertler no longer smells of sanctity in Kinshasa, particularly with the strong man of the capital, Félix Tshisekedi.
He is nothing less than the grandson of Moshe Schnitzer, considered one of the founding fathers of the Israeli diamond industry, whose fame today in the world is well established. Patriarch Schnitzer indeed co-founded the Israel Diamond Exchange and was even its first president.
While the civil war rages in Liberia, Dan Gertler is accused of having sold arms to various belligerents in exchange for diamonds, in violation of the international embargo. Allegations that Dan Gertler and his entourage still refute today.
It is a system that has proven itself since another Israeli billionaire, Beny Steinmetz, used it in Guinea to enrich himself thanks to the giant iron deposit of Mount Simandou. Dan Gertler applied the same method, but on a large scale.
In 2010, for example, he bought the Metalkol copper-cobalt mine for $ 60 million, wrested by the State from First Quantum Minerals. A few months later, he sold the asset for $ 685 million to Eurasian Natural Resources Corporation
Washington accuses him of causing the Congolese treasury to lose more than $ XNUMX billion.
«This is the first time that you, brothers and sisters, have gone to benefit from the wealth of this country.On every ton of copper or cobalt that is going to be minedeach Congolese will be a partner and paid for each tonne exported“, He explains, great lord.
